# Working with GitHub – Rules for Intergalactic Teacher

## Core Tools & Repos

- Use the GitHub CLI (`gh` command) for all GitHub interactions (issues, PRs, project boards)
- **Main repository:** [niros1/intergalactic-teacher](https://github.com/niros1/intergalactic-teacher)
- **Main project board:** [Project Board (niros1/intergalactic-teacher, project 2)](https://github.com/users/niros1/projects/2)

---

## Creating Issues

- Always relate new issues to the main project (project 2), starting in the **Backlog**.
- **Command example:**

  ```bash
  gh issue create --title "Your Issue Title" --body "Details here" --repo niros1/intergalactic-teacher \
    --project 'https://github.com/users/niros1/projects/2' --label backlog
  ```

---

## Working on Issues
- when starting to work on issue create a branch first
- DO NOT COMMIT CODE WITHOUT MY APPROVAL
---
## Project Workflows

- Move issues to the relevant project columns/stages as work progresses (e.g., In Progress, Done).
- Reference related issues and pull requests in commit messages and PRs for traceability.

---

## General Conventions

- Keep issues up to date with their status and ensure they're linked to the appropriate project board items.
- Always use appropriate labels (`bug`, `feature`, `enhancement`, etc.) for issues.

